            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">An 80-year-old man with limiting angina pectoris.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INVESTIGATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Physical examination, laboratory tests, echocardiography, exercise ECG, coronary arteriography, pressure wire assessment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DIAGNOSIS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Single severe calcific coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="TREATMENT" NlmCategory="METHODS">Elective percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) for calcific mid-vessel stenosis with rotational and excimer laser atherectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
